From a47c3a21a82fac05e5c3179e70469301f8218495 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aegis Development <development@example.invalid>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 20:40:41 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(android): bind Access Options editor to a menu grant in
 its window

Issue the editor only to the receiver created by a browser menu action, once
that receiver is attached to the tab window. The menu grant is one-use and is
bound to the receiver, tab contents, primary main frame and window, so revoked
or restored receivers cannot obtain a new editor through a direct native call.
Run the instrumentation by default in an internal-only APK that carries the
product identity and product template resources.

The regression skips the first run experience and recreates the real browser
Activity, so the restored receiver is the one Android rebuilds from saved
state rather than a dialog shown by the test.

The test library depends only on test support targets rather than
:chrome_test_java_helper, so the dedicated APK carries no other runnable suite.

The menu grant follows the existing trust boundary: configuration files,
Intents, deep links and Java-supplied channel values never grant privileges,
while browser-process code is trusted. It keeps revoked, restored or reused
receivers from obtaining an editor; it does not defend against same-process
callers.
